Menu="UserPreferences"
Title="Custom Header Logo"
Icon="image"
---
<?php
/* Custom Header Logo - replace the Unraid logo and its link in the top banner.
 * Settings are stored on the flash drive and survive reboots and OS updates.
 */
$chl_cfg_file = '/boot/config/plugins/custom.header.logo/custom.header.logo.cfg';
$chl_cfg = is_file($chl_cfg_file) ? (parse_ini_file($chl_cfg_file) ?: []) : [];
$chl_service = $chl_cfg['SERVICE']     ?? 'disabled';
$chl_logourl = $chl_cfg['LOGOURL']     ?? '';
$chl_linkurl = $chl_cfg['LINKURL']     ?? '';
$chl_height  = $chl_cfg['HEIGHT']      ?? '28';
$chl_newtab  = $chl_cfg['NEWTAB']      ?? '0';
$chl_showver = $chl_cfg['SHOWVERSION'] ?? '1';
?>

<form markdown="1" name="custom_header_logo" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="custom.header.logo/custom.header.logo.cfg"/>

_(Enable custom logo)_:
: <select name="SERVICE">
  <?=mk_option($chl_service, "disabled", _('No'))?>
  <?=mk_option($chl_service, "enabled", _('Yes'))?>
  </select>

> Set to **Yes** to replace the stock Unraid logo in the top banner. Set to **No** to restore the original logo (refresh the page after applying).

_(Logo image URL)_:
: <input type="text" name="LOGOURL" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($chl_logourl, ENT_QUOTES)?>" maxlength="1024" placeholder="https://example.com/logo.png or /boot/config/plugins/custom.header.logo/logo.png">

> URL of the image to display. PNG or SVG with a **transparent background** is recommended.
> **Suggested size: 320 x 56 px** (displayed at 160 x 28 px, matching the stock logo). Any image with a roughly 5.7:1 width/height ratio will look native; the height set below constrains it.
> You can also store the image on the flash drive (e.g. `/boot/config/plugins/custom.header.logo/logo.png`) and reference it as `/plugins/custom.header.logo/logo.png` after copying it into the plugin folder, or use any reachable http(s) URL.

_(Logo links to)_:
: <input type="text" name="LINKURL" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($chl_linkurl, ENT_QUOTES)?>" maxlength="1024" placeholder="https://example.com (empty = /Dashboard)">

> The page opened when the logo is clicked. Leave empty to link to the server Dashboard.

_(Logo height in pixels)_:
: <input type="number" name="HEIGHT" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($chl_height, ENT_QUOTES)?>" min="12" max="80" style="width:80px">

> Displayed height of the logo. Default **28** (stock logo height). Width scales automatically. The banner is 90 px tall, so values above 80 are clamped.

_(Open link in a new tab)_:
: <select name="NEWTAB">
  <?=mk_option($chl_newtab, "0", _('No'))?>
  <?=mk_option($chl_newtab, "1", _('Yes'))?>
  </select>

_(Keep Unraid version text next to logo)_:
: <select name="SHOWVERSION">
  <?=mk_option($chl_showver, "0", _('No'))?>
  <?=mk_option($chl_showver, "1", _('Yes'))?>
  </select>

> The stock logo component also displays the OS version. Hiding it removes that text; this option re-adds a small version label next to your custom logo.

&nbsp;
: <span class="inline-block">
  <input type="submit" name="#apply" value="_(Apply)_" disabled>
  <input type="button" value="_(Done)_" onclick="done()">
</span>

</form>

<p><em>Changes take effect after a page refresh. Settings are stored on the flash drive and re-applied automatically at every boot.</em></p>
